  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton has $1.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 258 awards with an average award size of $6.7M. Obligations are down 17.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show growth through FY25 and a partial pullback in FY26: FY21 was $466M, FY22 was $1.1B, FY23 was $1.7B, FY24 was $2B, FY25 was $2.1B, and FY26 is $1.7B. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date with $619M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $353M and the Department of Transportation with $210M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest NAICS market for Peraton in FY2026 to date with $831M, followed by Engineering Services with $380M and Custom Computer Programming Services with $152M. This profile shows concentration in systems, engineering, and IT services and a sizeable GSA relationship in the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Peraton's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Peraton obligated $1.7B in FY2026 to date, down 17.9% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $466M in FY21 to $2.1B in FY25, then declined to $1.7B in FY26 to date. The company issued 258 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $6.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Peraton's top agency customers and markets?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the top buyer with $619M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Defense with $353M and the Department of Transportation with $210M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top market at $831M, with Engineering Services at $380M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $152M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Peraton make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Peraton makes $1.7B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Peraton recorded 258 awards in the current fiscal year with an average award size of $6.7M, and obligations are down 17.9% year over year. Annual obligations moved from $466M in FY21 to $2.1B in FY25 before falling to $1.7B in FY26 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Peraton?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration, Department of Defense, and Department of Transportation are the largest buyers of Peraton in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $619M, the Department of Defense obligated $353M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $210M. Other buyers include NASA at $183M and HHS at $113M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Peraton sell to the government?",
      "a": "Peraton sells systems, engineering, and IT services to the government. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $831M, Engineering Services is $380M, and Custom Computer Programming Services is $152M in FY2026 to date. Peraton also has obligations in telecommunications, hosting and data processing, landscape architectural services, and R&D markets."
